WINDOWS B ENGRAM LANE PROCEDURE (Engram::Fable, 2026-11-26; rev 2 at 21:52Z added Opus2's WinB budget; rev 3 at 21:55Z added the WinB coordinator; rev 4 at 21:56Z adds the WinB cargo split agreed with Termal::Fable2 #8944), after Greg via Asistant 43498a6e:
- #2148, verbatim: „powtorze jeszcze raz, chcialbym przeniesc wiekszosc pracy na Windows B kodwanie, testy itp”;
- #2150, verbatim: „na windows B mozena zrobic drugiego koordynatora”;
- „Tak dla Engram na Window B.” (#2124);
- „oczywiscie, moze tego uzywac” (#2143: the Engram-runner clone, despite its disabled push URL).
ROLES: Engram::Fable (Central, session-5135) is the project coordinator. Engram::Fable-WinB (WinB session-24) is the LOCAL coordinator for Engram work on Windows B: it assigns WinB items, follows up, sees evaluation and closure through, grants Engram's WinB cargo slot, and is the SINGLE WRITER of WinB's .engram-data. It reports to Engram::Fable. It authors no code and gains no authority beyond AGENTS.md and this note. TermAl's WinB coordinator is Termal::Coord-WinB.
Every Engram coder session on Windows B follows this:
1. MODEL: Codex gpt-6.2-sol or Claude Opus, reasoning effort high (Greg). Only Sol or Opus author code.
2. WORK ONLY ITEMS ASSIGNED by Fable or Fable-WinB. Claim in the WinB store (C:\Users\Greg\.engram). Claims are host-local, and an item must never run on two hosts. Implement in your own worktree under C:\GitHub\Personal\Engram-runner\.worktrees\<item-short>-<session>.
3. CARGO ON WINB: inside Opus2's combined budget (#1887, memory winb-cargo-budget-2026-11-26: two -j2 runs, one FULL, FV floor), split with TermAl as agreed by Fable and Fable2 (#8944/#8945):
   - Engram gets ONE bounded run (CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2, own worktree and target) at a time;
   - the single WinB FULL slot alternates between the projects by request time, with at most one other bounded run beside a FULL;
   - a coder sends START to Fable-WinB and waits for its named grant, then sends END;
   - Fable-WinB mails Termal::Coord-WinB START and END for every Engram cargo run and FULL;
   - whoever starts checks FreeVirtualMemory >= 20,971,520 KiB;
   - kill nothing, no process listing.
   UNTIL Coord-WinB exists and Fable-WinB confirms the switch, Termal::Opus2 (host:8c5466d3-f0ef-4a01-99e9-b7b60c82b896::session-8111) still grants. Disputes go to Fable and Fable2.
   Use `node scripts/test-launcher.mjs focused --input commit -- …` for focused checks.
4. AUTHOR-TEST REF: push only your exact candidate commit with an explicit URL, never changing the clone's disabled push URL: git push https://github.com/grlap/Engram.git <commit>:refs/heads/author-test/<item>-<commit8>. First confirm the ref is absent and the parent is on origin. Never master, force, rebase or merge.
5. REVIEW: spawn the pair yourself on WinB (read-only Codex + read-only Claude via TermAl), on the frozen candidate. Fix in-scope Mediums. Land-then-fix applies to Mediums with no data loss, no security exposure and no broken criterion: file those as their own items. Scope rulings go to Fable-WinB, or to Fable when it's a cross-host or authority question.
6. FULL ON WINB: `node scripts/test-launcher.mjs full --input commit` on the clean candidate whose parent is current origin/master, in the granted FULL slot. A WinB FULL counts with equal weight. A Linux check, if needed, goes through Opus2's DL560 lane.
7. LANDING: send READY to Engram::Merger (host:8c5466d3-…::session-11859, Central) with the commit, source_id, FULL run id, the review rounds and the ref. The Merger lands (ff master) and installs.
8. EVALUATION AND CLOSURE ON WINB: the WinB store has independent_session (Greg „Wlącz dla Engram.”). Get the evaluation through TermAl on WinB, then run `done --landed <commit> ...` in the WinB store.
9. DATA SYNC: ONE writer of WinB's .engram-data, Fable-WinB once it has taken over by mail; until then, Codex-WinB-Coder2 (session-15), under a standing authorization. Coders mail the writer to sync after each author-ref push and after done. The writer imports the origin tip first, then exports, commits, confirm-imports and pushes engram-data fast-forward only with the explicit URL. Keep `.engram/** text eol=lf` in the clone's info/attributes until w-b534c27ad852 lands.
10. REPORT BY MAIL: coders send every milestone (claim, ref, pair end, FULL, READY, done) to Fable-WinB and to Engram::Fable (host:8c5466d3-…::session-5135) with termal_send_to_session, never only in a transcript. Fable-WinB sends Fable a summary at each landing or blocker. Cross-host mail always shows "durableButNotWoken" (TermAl w-0d2af77bed60); that's not a failure.
